  "context_pill": "Marginal Relief for Domestic Companies",
  "example_summary": "Computation of Marginal Relief for Y Ltd. for A.Y. 2026-27 when total income exceeds ₹ 10 crore.",
  "source_provision": "| Total Income Threshold | Applicable Base Tax Rate | Surcharge Rate |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Gross Receipts in Relevant PY ≤ ₹ 400 Crore | 25% | 0% (≤ ₹ 1 Cr) / 7% (> ₹ 1 Cr to ₹ 10 Cr) / 12% (> ₹ 10 Cr) |\n| Gross Receipts in Relevant PY > ₹ 400 Crore | 30% | 0% (≤ ₹ 1 Cr) / 7% (> ₹ 1 Cr to ₹ 10 Cr) / 12% (> ₹ 10 Cr) |\n\n**Statutory Conditions & Marginal Relief Steps:**\n\n* **Threshold Trigger:** Marginal Relief applies when Total Income slightly exceeds ₹ 1 Crore or ₹ 10 Crore, preventing higher surcharge from consuming excess income.\n* **Cap Rule:** Tax payable (including Surcharge) cannot exceed: `[Tax + Surcharge on ₹ 10 Crore] + [Total Income - ₹ 10 Crore]`.\n* **Relief Formula:** `Marginal Relief = Tax (incl. Surcharge) on Total Income - Maximum Permissible Tax before Cess`.\n* **Cess Application:** Health and Education Cess @ 4% is applied strictly *after* adjusting Marginal Relief.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Order of Computation Trap: Health and Education Cess @ 4% must ALWAYS be calculated on the net tax amount derived *after* granting Marginal Relief, never before.",
